// is the MCP-audience token: auth routing pins these methods to the MCP
// verifier (audience = the MCP resource URL), the anti-confusion
// boundary vs the main API audience, so a main-API token is rejected
// here and vice versa. The MCP handler forwards the caller's bearer so
// the full interceptor chain (auth → membership → permission) re-runs
// identically on whichever transport the call arrives over.
//
// PERMISSION MODEL. Every method here is `exempt` from the generated
// permission interceptor, and each data method enforces its read
// permission IN THE HANDLER instead. This is deliberate, not an
// oversight:
//
